IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-p3-subsidiary`

-- Tests for sgia-p3-subsidiary.l4 (ss 19 to 26A). Expected values are written from the text of each section.

§ `s 19`

#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may be amended, varied, rescinded or revoked at any time` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may be amended, varied, rescinded or revoked at any time` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may be amended, varied, rescinded or revoked at any time` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation may be amended, varied, rescinded or revoked at any time` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to fix the date includes the power to amend, revoke or suspend the subsidiary legislation fixing it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power to fix the date includes the power to amend, revoke or suspend the subsidiary legislation fixing it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to fix the date includes the power to amend, revoke or suspend the subsidiary legislation fixing it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the replacing authority may exercise the power over matters within its jurisdiction as if it were the original authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the replacing authority may exercise the power over matters within its jurisdiction as if it were the original authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the replacing authority may exercise the power over matters within its jurisdiction as if it were the original authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the enumeration of the special purposes derogates from the generality of the power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the enumeration of the special purposes derogates from the generality of the power` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the enumeration of the special purposes derogates from the generality of the power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made under an Act is permitted` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made under an Act is permitted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation made under an Act is permitted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 20`

#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to provide that a contravention is punishable by a fine and imprisonment within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to amend forms prescribed by the written law under which the subsidiary legislation was made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to prescribe new forms` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to provide for submitting, issuing or serving a document, record, application, permit, approval or licence by electronic means, or for its authentication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to provide for the manner and method of payment of fees and charges, and their reduction, waiver or refund` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to impose charges and penalties for late payment of fees and charges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `authority to impose interest on an outstanding fee, charge or penalty, or on payment by instalment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `authority to make subsidiary legislation also includes` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the limits: a fine not exceeding $2,000, imprisonment not exceeding 12 months, or both
#ASSERT `the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 2000 12
#ASSERT NOT (`the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 2001 12)
#ASSERT NOT (`the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 2000 13)
#ASSERT `the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 0 12
#ASSERT `the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 2000 0
#ASSERT `the penalty is within the limits of section 20(a)(i)` 1999 11
#ASSERT `the reference includes any subsidiary legislation made under the other written law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the reference includes any subsidiary legislation made under the other written law` FALSE)

§ `s 21, 22`

#ASSERT `expressions in the subsidiary legislation have the same meanings as in the Act conferring the power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `expressions in the subsidiary legislation have the same meanings as in the Act conferring the power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `expressions in the subsidiary legislation have the same meanings as in the Act conferring the power` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` TRUE TRUE `bringing the Act or part into operation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` TRUE TRUE `giving full effect to the Act or part on or after the day it comes into operation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` TRUE TRUE `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` FALSE TRUE `bringing the Act or part into operation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` TRUE FALSE `bringing the Act or part into operation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised after the passing of the Act so as to take effect at any time after it` TRUE TRUE `bringing the Act or part into operation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23`

#ASSERT `subsidiary legislation must be published in the Gazette` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`subsidiary legislation must be published in the Gazette` TRUE)
-- no date of its own: the date of publication; a date of its own governs
#ASSERT `the day subsidiary legislation takes effect and comes into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the day subsidiary legislation takes effect and comes into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
-- s 23(2): not earlier than the commencement of the Act, nor (where there is one) the establishment of the authority
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` (Date 31 12 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` (Date 1 1 2021) (Date 1 1 2020) (JUST (Date 1 1 2021))
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` (Date 30 6 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation may be made to operate retrospectively to that date` (Date 30 6 2020) (Date 1 7 2020) (JUST (Date 1 1 2020)))

§ `s 24, 25, 26, 26A`

#ASSERT `judicial notice is to be taken of the subsidiary legislation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`judicial notice is to be taken of the subsidiary legislation` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the amending subsidiary legislation is construed as one with the amended subsidiary legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amending subsidiary legislation is construed as one with the amended subsidiary legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amending subsidiary legislation is construed as one with the amended subsidiary legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amending subsidiary legislation is construed as one with the amended subsidiary legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the act is deemed to be done under the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed to be done under the Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under that Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under that Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the reference includes subsidiary legislation made under that Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
